::ENG4_U01_L04_GP_Q1::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which paraphrase is most accurate? {
~A. Modern libraries have replaced books with technology.#This distorts the passage.
=B. Modern libraries still value books but also support learning through services, tools, and spaces.#Correct. This preserves the balance.
~C. Libraries are only storage places for printed books.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Libraries no longer support reading.#This contradicts the passage.
}

::ENG4_U01_L04_GP_Q2::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which word best describes the sentence's academic focus? {
~A. Entertainment#The sentence focuses on learning support, not entertainment.
~B. Isolation#The sentence includes collaborative spaces.
~C. Replacement#The passage does not say one access type replaces another.
=D. Balance#Correct. The sentence emphasizes balancing different types of access.
}

::ENG4_U01_L04_GP_Q3::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. Which revision improves clarity and academic style? Original: Libraries help because stuff is there. {
=A. Libraries strengthen independent learning by reducing barriers to information and support.#Correct. This is clear, precise, and academic.
~B. Libraries help because stuff is there for people and it is good.#This remains vague.
~C. Libraries are helpful because of things.#This remains vague.
~D. Libraries help a lot, honestly.#This is informal and vague.
}

::ENG4_U01_L04_GP_Q4::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which sentence follows standard English conventions? {
~A. Reading, research, and community learning supports one another.#The compound subject needs support.
~B. Reading research and community learning support one another.#The series needs commas for clarity.
=C. Reading, research, and community learning support one another.#Correct. The subject and verb agree.
~D. Reading, research, and community learning, support one another.#The comma before the verb is incorrect.
}

::ENG4_U01_L04_GP_Q5::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which analytical claim is best supported? {
~A. The passage argues that printed books should be removed.#The passage says books remain important.
=B. The passage redefines libraries as active learning centers.#Correct. This claim is supported by the passage.
~C. The passage presents libraries as outdated institutions.#The passage presents libraries as expanded learning centers.
~D. The passage focuses only on quiet study space.#This is too narrow.
}
